 "notes": "From Fig. 3 top panel (linear coupling), 95% C.L. excluded region for |d_e^(1)|, the Damour-Donoghue dilatonic electromagnetic coupling. Paper defines alpha_EM(phi)=alpha_EM(1+d_e^(1) phi) with dimensionless phi; App. A gives phi=sqrt(4pi)*phi_dim/M_Pl=kappa*phi_dim, so d_e^(1) equals the canonical d_e (kappa=sqrt(4pi)/M_Pl) with no conversion. Curve is the lower envelope (boundary of the union of excluded regions) over the six SOLID experiment curves: SYRTE Rb/Cs (ref44) and Dy-VanTilburg (ref43) clock/oscillation limits at low mass, and static UFF limits Eot-Wash Be/Ti (ref40), Eot-Wash Cu/Pb-U (ref39), MICROSCOPE Ti/Pt (ref42). The dashed MICROSCOPE-osc line was EXCLUDED (paper states it is not an actual constraint but a sensitivity estimate). Low-mass (m<~1e-18 eV) part is the clock/oscillation limit which assumes the scalar is all DM at rho=0.4 GeV/cm^3 (Eq 28); the plateau and high-mass part come from UFF tests which are DM-density independent. The jagged SYRTE forest region was smoothed by per-log-mass-bin medians. Axes calibrated from figure gridlines/ticks; consistency cross-checked via m=h*f between the top (f) and bottom (m) axes. Values reported paper-native (no density rescaling).",
